  "definition": "Land surface temperature (LST) is the radiometric skin temperature of the surface components within a sensor's field of view. A forest pixel mainly represents the canopy; a bare-soil pixel represents the ground; sparse vegetation can mix soil and leaf temperatures. LST is distinct from the air temperature measured above the surface, although surface and atmosphere exchange heat and influence one another.[^1][^2]",
